Blocked: the pull request body holds a closing keyword inside backticks.

  source: the --body value

GitHub does not read Closes/Fixes/Resolves #N as a closing keyword inside a
code span or a code block, so merging the pull request leaves the issue open.

Fix: if the issue is meant to close on the merge, write the keyword bare:
  Closes #656
To quote or document the keyword instead, replace the real number with a
placeholder (`Closes #N` — without a number it is not detected).
